{
	"$comment": "Colors match src/app.css's light palette (--color-bg, --color-bg-elevated) — the manifest spec has no light/dark pair, so app.html carries the dark variant separately via <meta name=\"theme-color\" media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\">.",
	"id": "/",
	"name": "Glossa Catholica",
	"short_name": "Glossa",
	"description": "Scripture and the Magisterium — the Bible, the Catechism, the Compendium, and the documents of the Church. Free to read, offline-first.",
	"start_url": "/",
	"scope": "/",
	"display": "standalone",
	"background_color": "#ffffff",
	"theme_color": "#f6f5f1",
	"lang": "en",
	"$comment_categories": "Play and the desktop app stores read these; nothing on the web does.",
	"categories": ["books", "education"],
	"$comment_shortcuts": "Named in Latin because a shortcut label is ONE static string and the interface has 37 languages — there is no key to translate it by. Latin is the language the canonical reader URLs are already in (site/CLAUDE.md), so the label and the address it opens agree. /doctores is deliberately absent for the same reason it is absent from the nav: the Summa awaits a quality pass.",
	"shortcuts": [
		{ "name": "Scriptura", "url": "/scriptura" },
		{ "name": "Catechismus", "url": "/catechismus" },
		{ "name": "Calendarium", "url": "/calendarium" }
	],
	"icons": [
		{ "src": "/icons/icon-192.png", "sizes": "192x192", "type": "image/png", "purpose": "any" },
		{ "src": "/icons/icon-512.png", "sizes": "512x512", "type": "image/png", "purpose": "any" },
		{
			"src": "/icons/icon-maskable-512.png",
			"sizes": "512x512",
			"type": "image/png",
			"purpose": "maskable"
		},
		{
			"$comment": "Android 13+ themed icons. A SEPARATE entry, never a purpose merged into the ones above: a monochrome asset is an alpha silhouette the launcher tints itself, so anything declaring it as also \"any\" would ship a black-on-black icon to every surface that took the first purpose it understood. Generated from src/lib/assets/favicon.svg with both fills flattened, inset to match icon-maskable-512.png exactly (245x266 at +133,+123).",
			"src": "/icons/icon-monochrome-512.png",
			"sizes": "512x512",
			"type": "image/png",
			"purpose": "monochrome"
		}
	]
}
